  "notes": "Late at night, from a loft overlooking the garden, the world seems to have almost switched itself off.\nThis SPL Reference measurement captured a background level of around 30 dB — no traffic demanding attention, no conversations, no machinery; just the faint acoustic traces of an environment that feels virtually silent.\nAnd that is perhaps the interesting part: absolute silence is not zero decibels. Even when we perceive silence, there is still a measurable soundscape around us.\nA quiet reference point for the SPL Reference collection — and a reminder of just how different 30 dB feels after a day surrounded by the sound of the city.",
